[1m[38;5;231mWhich approach?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mA — tracking inside login (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mlogin does auth then fires the tracking POST fire-and-forget. Tracking can't be skipped. Couples auth to analytics;
[39m     [38;5;246mcheap to unwind later.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m B — tracking in the caller
     [38;5;246mlogin stays pure auth and returns userId; the submit handler calls trackLogin separately. Cleaner separation, but [39m
     [38;5;246mfuture callers can forget to track.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m C — loginAndTrack wrapper
     [38;5;246mCompose the two behind a wrapper. Both properties, but extra indirection I judged YAGNI for a 28-line file with one
